---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Cosme, Paros — Stayed & Reviewed | Suites With Keith"
  description="Keith's verdict on Cosme, Paros: the island's best beach stay, entry rooms bigger than most junior suites, and the room categories to skip."
  current="hotels"
  preload="/images/hotels/cosme-1.jpg"
>

<header class="hero" style="min-height:min(72svh,680px);">
  <img class="hero-img" src="/images/hotels/cosme-1.jpg" alt="Cosme, Paros — the pool terrace toward the sea" width="1800" height="1013" fetchpriority="high" />
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Hotel record &middot; Paros, Greece</p>
    <h1 class="display-xl" style="max-width:8ch;">Cosme</h1>
    <p class="stamp" style="margin-top:20px;">Stayed &middot; date pending verification</p>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- 1 · the verdict, first -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="verdict reveal">
      <p>Paros&rsquo; best beach stay. The laid-back luxury is genuinely refreshing, the rates are high &mdash; and the base rooms are massive, larger than many hotels&rsquo; junior suites, which is the rare entry category I&rsquo;d happily book.</p>
    </div>

    <dl class="kv reveal" style="margin-top:48px;">
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Wrong for</dt><dd>Anyone chasing the Mykonos scene &mdash; Naousa is lively, not flashy. And skip the plunge-pool rooms over the shared pool: they overlook the main infinity pool and aren&rsquo;t particularly private.</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Room to book</dt><dd><b>A base room, honestly</b> &mdash; they&rsquo;re enormous. Going bigger, the Cosmos Suite is the showpiece, but I preferred the Enastro for privacy.</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>When to go</dt><dd>May or September&ndash;October. Shoulder-season rates drop dramatically from peak summer.</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Beachfront with a private beach club out front &mdash; no shuttles, no sunbed battle &mdash; and Naousa&rsquo;s restaurants on foot.</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>My ranking</dt><dd>#09 of my Greece Top 10</dd></div>
      <div class="kv-row"><dt>Torn?</dt><dd><a href="/compare/cosme-vs-parilio.html" style="color:var(--brass); font-weight:400;">Cosme or Par&imacr;lio &mdash; the full head-to-head &rarr;</a></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 2 · what stood out -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">What stood out</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">The details that made the list</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="photos reveal" style="margin-bottom:44px;">
      <figure><img src="/images/hotels/cosme-1.jpg" alt="The pool terrace at Cosme" width="1800" height="1013" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>The pool terrace, toward the beach club</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/hotels/cosme-2.jpg" alt="A suite at Cosme, Paros" width="1800" height="1013" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>The base rooms &mdash; bigger than most junior suites</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="max-width:62ch;">
      <p style="margin-bottom:16px;">The circular spa and gym buildings are genuinely unique architecture, and both deliver. The private beach club sits directly in front of the hotel. And between the beach, spa and dining, you could stay four nights without getting bored &mdash; rare on the islands.</p>
      <p class="body-2">Despite what you may have heard, Paros is not &ldquo;the new Mykonos.&rdquo; Naousa is lively and fun without the flashy scene &mdash; a really easy, nicely rounded island. Cosme is exactly that as a hotel.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 3 · perks -->
<section class="section band on-shadow">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:820px; text-align:center;">
    <span class="eyebrow reveal" style="display:block; margin-bottom:16px;">Book Cosme through me</span>
    <h2 class="display-l reveal">Same rate &mdash; sometimes better.<br>Never the same welcome.</h2>
    <p class="body-2 reveal" style="margin:22px auto 0; max-width:52ch;">As a Fora advisor my clients receive a space-available upgrade, daily breakfast and a hotel credit &mdash; plus my direct line to the team on property before and during your stay.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 4 · the ask -->
<section class="section inquire" id="inquire">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="display-l reveal">When are you thinking?</h2>
    <p class="deck reveal" style="margin:18px auto 0; max-width:40ch;">I&rsquo;ve stood in these rooms. Tell me your dates and I&rsquo;ll match you to the right one, in the right season.</p>
    <form class="inquire-form reveal" action="https://formspree.io/f/mjgnadov" method="POST">
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Cosme Inquiry" />
      <input type="hidden" name="hotel" value="Cosme, Paros" />
      <input type="hidden" name="page" value="phase1/hotels/cosme-paros" />
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      <div class="step1">
        <label for="q-when">When are you thinking?</label>
        <input id="q-when" type="text" name="travel_dates" placeholder="Late June, 5 nights" required autocomplete="off" />
      </div>
      <div class="step2">
        <label for="q-name">And where do I send the recommendation?</label>
        <input id="q-name" type="text" name="name" placeholder="Name" required autocomplete="name" />
        <input id="q-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="Email" required autocomplete="email" />
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Send</button>
      <p class="note">Traveling within the next 30 days? You&rsquo;ll hear from me today.</p>
      <p class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
